A large pool of hitpoints makes regeneration more useful, because it can 
be working for a longer time after the fight. Look at the extreme: with 
only 1 hp, regeneration is totally worthless. The more hp you have, the 
more often you'll be actively regenerating.

It's good for a monk in particular because individual fights tend to 
last longer than with other classes (in my experience). Again, more time 
for regeneration to be active.

600 hp should be enough to survive anything. Yet I was down to 82 hp at 
the end, and wouldn't've lasted much longer. I don't know how I lost 
them so fast; my wizard ascension had 150 max hp. I make no claims to 
being good.

